Independent audit of completed cohort executions
================================================

This is new Source. It does not restore the unavailable historical frontend
whose handoff hash began 33c6. The unchanged registrar remains a separate,
Root-only administrative action after the audit succeeds.

Root reads the complete auditor, reader, guards, configuration, this protocol,
and a distinct independent Source review. Root then issues a fresh positive
decision from ROOT_DECISION_TEMPLATE_FALSE.json. The template itself grants
no authority. One positive decision names the exact cohort and metadata
attempt map; all four batch audits and the aggregate share that decision.

Execution order
---------------

Execute one guarded audit for each cohort batch, in order. Its output
directory must already exist and contain neither of the proposed output
files. The guard directory must be fresh. The exact child interface is::

  PY -E -B -S audit_actuals.py --config PATH BYTES SHA \
    --Root-decision PATH BYTES SHA --batch N --out DIRECTORY --guard GUARD

Use the existing environment with the five coverage/OpenSSL variables removed
and supervise_validation.py with the unchanged metadata limits: 256 MiB,
125 seconds, admission 4 GiB RAM/10 GiB disk, floors 3 GiB RAM/8 GiB disk.
Retain each genuine SDK record and every original issued/frame transport.

After every batch is terminal, execute the same child without --batch and
append one ordered occurrence of each of the following three arguments per
batch::

  --batch-review PATH BYTES SHA
  --batch-SDK PATH BYTES SHA
  --batch-key GENUINE_RAW_TRANSPORT_DIRECTORY_NAME

The aggregate checks the successful guarded execution that produced each
batch leaf and its full report. It does not rerun that batch's scientific or
metadata checks. Earlier reports retain their own exact first/closing IO
scope. The aggregate authenticates their selected output bytes and current
frozen snapshot, pairing and certificate pins.

Output and registrar interface
------------------------------

Each invocation exclusively writes full_actual_review.json and
reuse_integer_only.json. Batch leaves use F009_COHORT_BATCH_ACTUAL_REUSE_V1;
the final leaf uses F009_CONTIGUOUS_PARENT_COHORT_ACTUAL_REUSE_V1. Their
bindings retain supplier_cover_index=0 and the explicit zero-based strict
cover index. The old registrar consumes these leaves without treating a
single supplier certificate as equal to the entire three-parent certificate.

The claimed strict156 verification is borrowed from the freshly completed,
unchanged strict worker whose genuine API/guards/outputs are audited. The
auditor evaluates no forest, group, orbit, witness, rejection or graph
predicate. It checks scalar provenance, lexical record-slot indices, counts,
and opaque cover bytes. A lexical span parser exposes object names and
element boundaries; the denylist prevents decoding payload fields through
the selected-metadata interface. Whole canonical certificates and individual
cover spans have separately checked equality. Original parent/forest and
permutation arrays remain opaque inside these actual audit executions.

