Resource accounting
-------------------

Every invocation is independently bounded: file 4 MiB, 512 physical paths,
64 MiB total explicit reads, 256 MiB RSS, 125 seconds hard alarm and 115
seconds cooperative work. The exact first/closing input reads include the
auditor, reader, guard Sources, Source/authority documents, current frozen
snapshot and the selected cut's actual evidence. Reading the checked reader
before importing it is counted separately as bootstrap bytes.

The program reserves 2 MiB of aggregate read capacity for first/closing
verification of its two exclusively created output files, and includes two
output paths in the path admission check. Actual read bytes must stay below
the declared total. No recursive filesystem scan occurs in the actual
auditor. Missing SDKs, raw frames, physical inputs, guard evidence or closing
bytes are fatal; there is no missing-input skip.

The code namespace is the complete new auditor, exact reader, both existing
guards and 512 invocation bytes. The Source manifest records the exact
size; production scientific Sources are read as inert inputs and never
imported. A borrowed earlier report is not reclassified as newly executed
code. The guard's established sampling and detached-process qualifications
remain in force.

The present layer permits first-v1 scientific roles. Its metadata attempt
interface admits zero or more explicit overrides; prior refusal SDKs must have genuine
raw frames and exactly the selected argv. A scientific pre-entry retry needs
a separately reviewed extension. Cohort begin/end/partition and control
directory derive from the explicit cohort descriptor. The current application
is cohort330..341, whose closer has one genuine override. That exact closer
does not produce an all-v1 summary: later zero-override cohorts require a
compatible, separately reviewed closer. A new Source-owner schema also needs
explicit reviewed admission. These are metadata-interface requirements;
the scientific Sources remain unchanged.
